WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:29.499
In hypoplastic left heart syndrome, the left
side of a newborn’s heart hasn’t developed

00:00:29.499 --> 00:00:30.960
completely.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:37.830
The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood
containing the oxygen and nutrients that the

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.040
body needs.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:51.260
The pumping sections of the heart are the
right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.989
and left ventricle.

00:00:52.989 --> 00:01:00.600
In a normal heart, oxygen-poor blood flows
from the body through large veins called the

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.740
superior vena cava and inferior vena cava
into the right atrium.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:13.860
Next, blood moves into the right ventricle,
which contracts, sending blood to the lungs

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.940
through the pulmonary artery.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:22.960
Blood picks up oxygen in the lungs and returns
through the pulmonary veins to the left atrium

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.810
and then moves to the left ventricle.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:32.689
Finally, the left ventricle contracts, sending
oxygen-rich blood to the body through the

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:35.590
aorta.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:40.570
Before birth, the heart doesn’t send blood
to the lungs to get oxygen since the baby

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.920
isn’t breathing yet.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:48.939
Instead, all the oxygen the baby needs passes
from the mother’s blood to the baby through

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:53.580
the placenta and umbilical cord.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:02:01.940
In addition, blood from the baby’s heart
bypasses the lungs in two ways: one is through

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:11.400
a connection between the pulmonary artery
and the aorta called the ductis arteriosus.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:18.090
The other is through an opening in the wall
between the two atria called the foramen ovale.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:24.130
These extra openings allow oxygen-rich blood
to bypass the baby’s lungs and still circulate

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:26.420
through the body.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:33.819
Normally, within a day or two after birth,
both the ductis arteriosus and the foramen

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:44.300
ovale close, forcing the baby’s blood to
travel to the lungs to pick up oxygen.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:49.980
In hypoplastic left heart syndrome, a newborn
baby’s heart has severe birth defects that

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.770
prevent blood from flowing normally to the
rest of the body.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:59.190
If the body can’t get oxygen and nutrients,
it can’t survive.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:06.069
The left ventricle, which is the main pump,
and the aorta, which is the main pipeline,

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:11.280
are smaller than normal, so the baby’s body
does not receive enough blood.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:19.690
If the foramen ovale and ductis arteriosus
are allowed to close as they would normally,

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:28.290
bloodflow to the body would decrease even
more, resulting in a life-threatening situation.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:34.140
Symptoms of hypoplastic left heart syndrome
include: gray or bluish skin color and rapid

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:39.260
breathing as the baby tries to get more oxygen
to the body.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:44.250
Without surgical intervention, this condition
is fatal.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:50.740
Surgeons will perform three separate operations
to treat hypoplastic left heart syndrome.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:56.540
The goal of these operations is to improve
the flow of oxygen-rich blood to the baby’s

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:57.680
body.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:03.319
The Stage One operation, called the Norwood
procedure is performed during the first week

00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:05.900
after birth.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:09.590
During the operation, the surgeon will make
three main changes.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:16.209
First, the pulmonary artery will be separated
from the right and left pulmonary arteries

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:18.310
and connected to the aorta.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:24.710
A small piece of tubing called a graft will
be inserted to connect a branch of the aorta

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.610
and the right pulmonary artery.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:34.530
Finally, the surgeon will remove the wall
between the right and left atria.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:39.880
These changes increase the flow of oxygen-rich
blood from the lungs through both atria into

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:47.720
the right ventricle, increase the bloodflow
to the body through the new aorta, and increase

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:52.690
the bloodflow to the lungs through the graft.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:58.750
The Stage Two operation called the Glenn procedure
is performed about 6-months later when the

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.750
baby is stronger.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:06.690
The surgeon will remove the graft connecting
the branch of the aorta and the right pulmonary

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.470
artery.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:13.889
To replace the graft’s function, the surgeon
will disconnect the Superior vena cava from

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:19.150
the heart and reconnect it to the right pulmonary
artery.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:26.090
This connection allows oxygen-poor blood from
the head and arms to go directly to the lungs

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:30.449
to pick up oxygen.

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:36.370
The Stage Three operation called the Fontan
procedure is performed when the baby is 18-months

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.610
to three-years old.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:44.790
The surgeon will disconnect the Inferior vena
cava from the heart and reconnect it to the

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.590
R. pulmonary artery with graft tubing.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:53.690
This connection allows oxygen-poor blood from
the lower body to go directly to the lungs

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:58.410
to pick up oxygen.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:04.250
The Fontan procedure completes the surgical
repair of the heart by completing these goals:

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:09.730
delivery of oxygen-rich blood to the body
through the creation of a new and expanded

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:17.190
aorta, creation of a new path for oxygen-poor
blood to reach the lungs, and prevention of

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:23.979
the mixing of oxygen-rich blood and oxygen-poor
blood.

00:06:23.979 --> 00:06:29.569
These three operations relieve the life-threatening
condition caused by hypoplastic left heart

00:06:29.569 --> 00:06:36.770
syndrome but do not restore normal circulation
through the heart.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:42.990
In some cases, a heart transplant may be done
if a donor heart is available or the changes

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:49.400
from the three surgical procedures aren’t
working.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:54.580
After any of these operations, the child may
receive blood thinner medication to prevent

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.039
the formation of blood clots.

00:06:57.039 --> 00:07:02.410
Those with heart transplants will also need
medication to prevent their body from rejecting

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.420
the new heart.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.990
The child may need these medications for the
rest of their life.

